# Tinybones, Bauble Burglar's "During your turn, you may play cards you don't own with stash counters on them from exile, and
# mana of any type can be spent to cast those spells" is a static ability: it applies only while Tinybones is on the
# battlefield (CR 604.1, 611.3a), and the mana is spent after the cast's chance to activate mana abilities (CR 601.2g-h,
# 609.4b). Bot1 casts the stashed Lightning Bolt and, in the cast's mana window, has Ashnod's Altar sacrifice Tinybones for
# {C}{C}: Tinybones is gone when the cost is paid, so the {C}{C} can't pay the {R} and the window stays open - with the
# permission still applying it would have closed by itself, the pool covering the cost. Mox Ruby's {R} pays it, and the
# {C}{C} is left in the pool. (With Tinybones still there, other mana pays: the Mox Pearl scenario beside this one.)
# Turn 1: Swamp and Mox Ruby for Tinybones. Turn 3: Tinybones's ability makes Bot2 discard the Bolt, exiled with a stash
# counter. Turn 5: three Swamps for the Altar, then the Bolt.

